Endpoint Protection

+-- Endpoint solutions --+

Helps manage and protect various types of endpoints from cyberthreats + aditional plugins

The first endpoint security solution is the endpoint protection platform, or EPP.
This developed from the need of administrators to ensure servers and desktops are patched and have the appropriate antivirus
software installed.

Moderns EPPs can:

- Verify versions of software and firmware
- Scan the local system for viruses and malware
- Enforce data loss prevention and other company-defined security policies

///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////7

Another endpoint solution is nedpoint detection and response, or EDR. 
This is a more proactive security solution that constantly scans a device to detect indicators of compromise, or IOC.
If the EDR client detects a suspicious connection, program, or behaviour, it can block the action and send an alert.
This can help identify and stop threats like ransomware and zero-day attacks that may not have an established signature
that would be detected by traditional anti-malware systems.

EDR usually leverages A.I and large comprehensive databases of known attacks to predict and recognize suspicious files and programs.
ECR CAN TRIGGER ALERST TO OTHER CONNECTED ENDPOINTS and allow other endpoints to immediately block the suspicious behaviour.
Has tools to help gather data on new threats, and quarantine systems that are suspected of compromise.

